--- prim-handl — the pure-handl implementation of the `prim` contract
--- (`handl-packages/prim/prim.hnl`).
---
--- `prim` is the minimal FFI layer for handl's arrow-based stdlib: the
--- smallest set of atoms that cannot be expressed as handl arrow graphs.
--- Of the four declared `prim.*` functions, two are expressible over the
--- eval vocabulary (`add`, `alloc`) and are implemented here as pure
--- handl; two remain native `op`s registered by `plugin-lib-prim`:
---
---   - `prim.add` — pure handl: `[a, b] ~> a + b` over the builtin `+`.
---   - `prim.alloc` — pure handl: `n ~> []`. The contract guarantees
---     `LengthEq(output, 0)` — an empty list — so no list-size primitive
---     is needed.
---   - `prim.compare` — NATIVE: it is a deep total order over arbitrary
---     values (kind ordering null < bool < number < string < array <
---     object, with recursive array/object comparison). The language has
---     no runtime kind-introspection (`typeof` was removed from the
---     language surface), no string-ordering primitive (`lt`/`gt` are
---     numeric-only), and no object-key enumeration — so a handl
---     encoding is not possible without contorting the calculus.
---   - `prim.or` — NATIVE: bitwise OR for flag composition. The eval
---     vocabulary has no bitwise primitive (`or` is boolean truthiness),
---     and bitwise ops cannot be synthesized without a division/modulus
---     bit-extraction loop that would still lack a primitive shift.
---
--- Registered as the `"prim"` module by `plugin-lib-prim`
--- (`PrimModule`/`PrimLibraryPlugin`): the record fields `add`/`alloc`
--- become callables, and `with_ops` attaches the remaining native ops
--- (`prim.compare`, `prim.or`).

{
  -- prim.add — integer addition.
  add: [a, b] ~> a + b,

  -- prim.alloc — allocate an empty list (contract: LengthEq(output, 0)).
  alloc: n ~> []
}
